# =============================================================================
# QuantumHarmony distributed repository ignore baseline
# quantumharmony-ignore-baseline: 1
# =============================================================================
# Keep the shared block portable across repositories. Repository-specific
# runtime paths and deliberate exceptions belong after the END marker.
#
# Policy:
# - Ignore machine-local state, credentials, caches, generated output, and
#   mutable runtime data.
# - Keep source, schemas, migrations, fixtures, example configuration,
#   dependency lockfiles, and provenance archives visible by default.
# - Add narrow repository exceptions instead of broad rules such as **/data/,
#   *.jar, *.zip, or vendor/, which can hide legitimate shared resources.

# === BEGIN QUANTUMHARMONY SHARED BASELINE v1 ===

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operating-system metadata
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon?
._*
.DocumentRevisions-V100/
.Spotlight-V100/
.TemporaryItems/
.Trashes/
.fseventsd/
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
**.smbd*
